 Key Changes and Explanations: 

 HTML Modifications 

 Button Text and data-bs-toggle : 

 All instances of "Get Started Now", "Try ASTRA", and the navigation item "Get Started" have been changed to "Schedule Demo". 

 Crucially, these buttons now have data-bs-toggle="modal" and data-bs-target="#scheduleDemoModal" attributes. These are Bootstrap attributes that tell the button to open the modal with the ID scheduleDemoModal when clicked, instead of navigating to an anchor. 

 Modal Structure: 

 A new div with the Bootstrap modal structure has been added just before the closing </body> tag. 

 It includes modal-dialog , modal-content , modal-header , modal-body , and modal-footer classes for proper styling and functionality. 

 The id="scheduleDemoModal" is essential for the data-bs-target attribute to work. 

 Form within Modal: 

 The form ( <form id="demoForm"> ) is placed inside the modal-body . 

 It uses Bootstrap's form styling classes ( mb-3 , form-label , form-control ) to maintain consistency with your existing design. 

 The input fields for name , email , and message are included, along with the hidden botcheck field for Web3Forms. 

 The access_key input field now has an id="web3forms_access_key" so we can set its value using JavaScript. 

 The submit button has class="btn btn-schedule-demo" and a custom style to match your gradient buttons. 

 A div with id="result" is added to display submission messages. 

 CSS Additions 

 I've added specific CSS rules to style the new modal elements to ensure they blend seamlessly with your existing color scheme and typography: 

 .modal-content : Sets a dark background ( var(--secondary) ), rounded borders, and a subtle shadow. 

 .modal-header , .modal-title , .modal-body , .modal-footer : Styles for borders, text color, and padding within the modal. 

 .modal-header .btn-close : Inverts the color of the close button so it's visible on the dark background. 

 .form-label , .form-control : Styles for the form labels and input fields, using transparent backgrounds and light text for a consistent look. 

 .btn-schedule-demo : Applies your gradient background and button styling to the modal's submit button. 

 #result : Basic styling for the success/error message. 

 JavaScript Modifications 

 $('a[href^="#"]') update: I've modified the smooth scrolling script to not prevent the default behavior if the <a> tag has a data-bs-toggle attribute. This ensures that clicking a "Schedule Demo" button (which has data-bs-toggle="modal" ) will open the modal instead of attempting to scroll. 

 Web3Forms Integration Script: 

