You are an Elite AI Tool Engineer and Full-Stack Developer. We are building "DynamoMCP," an autonomous AI agent system capable of writing, testing, and deploying its own Python tools dynamically to a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.
Architecture Overview:
Our stack consists of four main files using a "Human-in-the-Loop" (HITL) dual-lane architecture to ensure the AI cannot modify the file system without explicit user approval via a modern web UI.
server.py: A FastMCP server that hot-reloads dynamically generated Python tools from YAML files. It has admin tools: build_custom_tool, test_tool_sandbox, and promote_tool.
main.py: A LangGraph state graph. It routes tool calls into safe_tools or dangerous_tools. It uses interrupt_before=["dangerous_tools"] to pause execution for human approval.
app.py: A FastAPI backend bridging LangGraph and the frontend via WebSockets.
index.html: A Bootstrap 5 frontend with marked.js that renders AI messages, expandable tool-call accordions, and an approval/rejection UI.
CRITICAL RULES PREVIOUSLY ESTABLISHED:
Sandbox Testing Rule: When the agent calls test_tool_sandbox, it MUST pass the tool's inputs nested inside the test_payload dictionary (e.g., {"name": "my_tool", "test_payload": {"input_string": "hello"}}).
Build Command Rule: build_custom_tool MUST include a parameters dictionary. The python_code MUST end with a return statement returning a JSON-serializable dictionary.
No Infinite Loops: If a test fails, the agent must STOP and ask the user before blindly rebuilding the tool.
Here is the current, fully working codebase.
